#pragma once
// Byte-exact SML telegram from the meter in the basement, captured through the
// IR read head on a USB-to-TTL adapter (tools/ir_head_test.py --dump). It is the
// layout the SML books do not describe and the reason the framer's buffer was
// too small: 620 bytes of payload, the 5-byte end marker, ONE FILLER BYTE, then
// the CRC - which covers that filler byte as well - and the whole thing once a
// second, 636 bytes at a time.
//
// Anonymised: the meter's serial number (server id "EFR" + 5 bytes, three
// occurrences) is replaced with 00 00 12 34 56 and the CRC recomputed. The
// serial is printed on the meter and identifies the household; the parser does
// not depend on it. The ` D7 63 ` in the sketch below is the original CRC.
//
//   ... 00 00 | 1B 1B 1B 1B 1A | 01 | D7 63 | 1B 1B 1B 1B 01 01 01 01 ...
//              \___ end marker ___/  ^    ^
//                                     |    +- CRC-16/X.25, low byte first,
//                                     |       covering the filler byte too
//                                     +------ filler byte
